methylKit can use BED files or properly formatted GRangesList objects when doing annotation. if you run the examples for read.transcript.features you can see what kind of GRangesList object is returned and try to tailor what you can from the annotation hub or any other format to that. It is basically a named list, where names correspond to genomic features, such as exon/promoter/intron etc.

Best,
Altuna

