When analyzing differentially methylated regions with Methylkit, you need to specify the percent methylation difference, for example larger than 25%  (myDiff25p.hyper <- get.methylDiff(myDiff, difference = 25, qvalue = 0.01, type = "hyper")

Does this mean that the control and test group need to differ at least 25% in absolute methylation, for example 50% against 75% methylation, or does it mean that the methylation values need to differ at least 25% relative against each other, thus 50% and 62,5% ?

Thank you for your help.

